    "ramp-brand-50": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "oklch(98.7% 0.0061 258)",
      "$extensions": {
        "silvicom.section": [
          "── brand hue, rotated +21 degrees (D-DR1, 2026-09-16) ────────────────────────────────────────\nThe 2026-09-15 comps were sampled and converted to OKLCH before anything was changed, and the finding was that the ENTIRE colour gap between this product and those comps is one number. Lightness and chroma already matched to within a rounding error (`action-primary` ours 55.2%/0.224 against the comp's 52.1%/0.2295); only the hue differed, 264 against 285. So this is a rotation at constant L and C, which is the reason it is safe: no WCAG pair that passes today can fail afterwards, and `lint:ui-contrast` is what proves it rather than this comment. A second thing falls out of the same measurement — the NEUTRALS here have always sat at hue 286. Brand at 264 was the odd one out, and brand and neutral now share a hue family for the first time.\n\nDeliberately NOT rotated: `viz-cost-reefer` and the rest of the D-FRUI8 cost palette. Those were tuned as a validated SET (lightness band, chroma floor, colour-vision separation, 3:1 on surface) and rotating one member broke it — `lint:chart-colors` caught it the same afternoon. Charts are DR3's business, on purpose.",
          "brand = warm gold identity. Interactive actions use their own graphite role."
        ],
        "silvicom.expose": "color"
      }
    },
